{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793314650,"nonce":"tYJk27l9jB+XHzomCG+giqSZ5+8=","title":"AOT dynamic-call stack capture crashes on Linux x86-64 (Haxe Issue6871)","message":"Release v0.1.14 / main 35374160, current AOT implementation 909f1977. Previous CI conformance run 40924250528 at a8f4140a records unit.issues.Issue6871 as CRASH exit -11; the current release CI has a reported crashing case and its full artifact is still pending. macOS arm64 passes the case.\n\nReduced to reflected static getter/setter functions that throw. On NUC Linux x86-64, compile with ash --build reflect reflect.hl and run: getter caught, then SIGSEGV on the setter. No external HDLL is needed; the reproducer links the current static runtime.\n\nGDB: libgcc_s -\u003e _Unwind_Backtrace -\u003e aot_capture_stack -\u003e capture_exception_stack -\u003e hlp_throw -\u003e Haxe setter -\u003e ash_static_call -\u003e bogus frame 0x1 -\u003e hlp_call_method -\u003e hlp_dyn_call -\u003e Reflect.setProperty -\u003e main.\n\nRoot cause: the System V inline assembly in std/src/fun.rs subtracts 32 from rsp around an indirect call, but the compiler-generated DWARF CFA does not describe that change. Linux exception-stack capture walks DWARF and reads outgoing argument words as saved return addresses. The same omission can truncate the getter's stack instead of crashing when the read happens to be zero. macOS arm64's frame-pointer walk does not expose this x86-64 path.\n\nFix in progress: put the call in an assembly helper with a stable rbp-based frame and complete CFI, retaining independent integer/float register banks, stack arguments, and rax/xmm0 results. The minimal getter/setter reproducer now catches both on the NUC. Add static/shared AOT regressions for captured caller frames, throwing with stack-spilled arguments, and integer/f32/f64 return values, and run the Linux upstream conformance cases again.","files":null}]}